    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To move from 2NF to 3NF, you need to address any transitive dependencies. A transitive dependency exists when a non-key attribute depends on another non-key attribute, rather than directly on the primary key. You can fix this by decomposing the table into multiple smaller tables, each containing the attributes that are dependent on a single determinant. This process, by isolating the dependency, ensures that the data is stored only once, which is the goal of achieving 3NF. Remember, this decomposition must preserve the original data relationships in the new structure.",
